<!--
  Emoji (T-359): a tenth language for fun, under the private-use language code qaa. Every string is
  written in emoji; placeholders stay data, and dates, numbers and amounts format as English.

  The same concept takes the same emoji everywhere, and the strings both clients show are
  identical to web/src/i18n/messages/qaa.ts. Letters appear only where every language keeps them:
  the app's name, the transliteration and the licence line, and "(Language)" after the picker's
  label, which is the way back for someone who picked a language they cannot read.
-->
